WEBVTT

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.190
Where's the slasher?

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.110
Take a look.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.860
Where's Shinyao?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.610
Wasn't she inside the building?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.660
We searched every floor.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:19.850
Wayne?

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.540
Guess we're starting from 
scratch with your friend.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.820
I didn't mean to kill him.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:27.780
It's okay.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.010
You did everything you could to protect me.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.260
I'm really happy. Thanks.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.350
So, did he leave any clues?

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.560
No. There was just this coat 
by the time we arrived.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.520
Yeah, that's right.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.370
<i>Sha Rijan.</i>

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.330
<i>A hundred years ago,</i>

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.360
<i>she was the strongest hunter 
of the shadows that dominated London.</i>

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.210
<i>She was what you'd call an Umbra Hunter.</i>

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.920
<i>It's likely she became internationally famous</i>

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.620
<i>after she fought and killed Count Dracula,</i>

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:41.180
<i>the powerful Umbra who had London 
in a whirlpool of fear at the time.</i>

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.930
<b>Episode 3 Twisted Bond</b>

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:43.510
Dracula?

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:49.610
<i>By the way, they say when 
she fought Count Dracula</i>

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.860
<i>she was always accompanied 
by a powerful jiangshi.</i>

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.820
Everyone's so powerful.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.610
I was Rijan-sama's tool 
before arriving in London.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:01.910
Her tool?

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:07.250
<i>While Sha Rijan should've been 
an Umbra's worst nightmare,</i>

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:11.040
<i>her philosophy was different 
from other Umbra hunters.</i>

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.750
<i>She sought not to eradicate Umbra,
 but to coexist with them.</i>

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:17.480
Coexist?

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:23.160
Respecting each other's territory 
without drawing lines too sharply.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:28.070
A world where humans and shadows 
could eventually coexist peacefully.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.600
That was the guiding principle of Rijan-sama

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:35.480
and the Twilights Organization 
she founded with her allies.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.930
Rijan established Café Forbidden

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.280
so humans could become accustomed to Umbra.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.460
<i>That's what I've gathered about the 
history of the secret organization</i>

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.000
<i>called Twilights from documents 
written at the time.</i>

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:56.360
If you want to know more,
 Rijan-san's study is on the top floor.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.130
Look there.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.590
I can't keep up.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.800
I can't believe my great-grandmother was the 
leader of such a questionable organization.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.800
It's not questionable.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.950
Unlike a hundred years ago, 
now we have international support.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.650
We have ties to governments 
and law enforcement in various countries.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.320
Now I really can't keep up.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:25.550
In any case, the Twilights 
will rescue your friend

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.490
and prove that humans 
and Umbra can get along.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:35.830
But Shinyao was kidnapped by Umbra.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.770
Just as there are those who seek 
harmony between humans and Umbra,

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:43.590
naturally there are those 
who think differently.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.300
The hawks, basically.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:51.770
They desire prosperity for Umbra 
and sow confusion among humans.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.890
In other words, those people...

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:58.860
No, the Umbra hate my great-grandmother.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.070
I was their real target.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.600
Well...

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.870
Shinyao was kidnapped because 
of me and my family.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.780
That's not true.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:15.840
There's no need for you to shoulder 
the hatred of an entire family.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.580
Luke-san?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.000
You're having negative thoughts 
because you're hungry.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.710
Eat some of this and cheer up.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.700
Luke, how many times do I have to tell 
you to keep that away from my tea?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.280
You should have some garlic once in a while.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.310
It'll give you energy.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.730
It would have the opposite effect.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.150
Besides, I'm an immortal vampire.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:43.530
Can you call yourself a vampire when you 
haven't sucked anyone's blood in a hundred years?

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.450
What?

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.740
Blood is no different than seawater.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.740
Nutritionally speaking, 
it's not strictly necessary.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:56.190
Isn't that a total rejection 
of your kind's identity?

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:03.500
Eat.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.740
You made this?

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:06.760
It's not poisoned.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.860
I don't want to harm humans.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.840
You're telling me that now,
 after I thought I was going to die?

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.790
Are you going to eat or not?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.440
I get what you're trying to say,

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.230
but the guy who taught me 
to cook was careless.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:30.280
He taught me ratios and 
seasoning based on feel.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.270
You don't have to force yourself.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:40.000
I'm not. Overall, it's good.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.540
What does that mean?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.710
I was just thinking it's true when 
they say hunger is the greatest spice.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.650
Will I get to see Ton?

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.140
You will.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.550
She'll come to see you.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.360
I thought you were sleeping upstairs.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.560
I couldn't sleep.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.620
You haven't slept in two days.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.260
My jet lag just disappeared.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:18.370
Don't worry about it. It's not your fault.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.780
Not that me telling you that 
would make you accept it.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.920
The more others protect you, 
the more it hurts.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:33.890
The more you're told you're not responsible, 
the more you feel responsible.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.810
You wish people would leave you alone.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:42.810
It makes you want to tell people you'll 
decide for yourself if it's your fault.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:50.440
Can I really interpret this as you trying 
to cheer me up rather than pick me up?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.900
Of course.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.980
I don't go after weakened girls.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:57.860
The real battle begins once you've recovered.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.120
Doesn't that lower your odds?

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.430
Don't say that. It's a question of policy.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.050
Hey, miss.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:12.350
Not as a Twilight, but as myself,

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.780
I promise I'll rescue your friend.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.350
That won't happen.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.560
Rescuing Shinyao is my right.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.650
What? Tch.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.950
<i>I did some research on Snowmary.</i>

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:42.160
Snowmary. That's the company 
that developed the app.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:46.670
<i>Yeah, but I can't find anything recent.</i>

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.570
They were founded three years ago.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.340
Their main office is here in London.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.410
In addition to the Magic Mirror app,

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:59.250
they've developed search apps, 
map apps, and health apps.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.060
They're a promising company 
that's growing rapidly.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:07.890
So they combined all that technology 
to predict people's actions.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.520
Who's behind them?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:16.030
I looked at their capital ties and banks, 
but didn't find anything suspicious.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:21.890
It doesn't make any sense
 in the first place that a rising IT company

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.720
would be working with Umbra.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.560
You're right.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.230
They enjoy terrorizing humans.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:32.300
Running a proper company in human 
society has to be some kind of joke.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.260
What should I do?

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.510
Should I keep looking into it?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.810
Do that. I'll try something else.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:38.240
Chris.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.950
Hey. It's been a while...

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.830
Brother.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.170
Where's the hostage?

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:00.880
Where's Baileu Ton?

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.300
Not here. I came alone.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.310
That wasn't our agreement, bro.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:10.730
The hostage in exchange for Baileu Ton.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.370
Isn't that what I told you?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.740
Why, Chris? Why do you hate humans?

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:20.710
Our home wasn't destroyed by humans.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.990
It was Umbra we believed were our allies.

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:27.830
Yeah. We were branded traitors and purged

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:32.460
because of the real traitors, 
influenced by human society.

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:37.090
Why do you hate humans when 
you understand all that?

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:40.380
You're the one who doesn't 
understand, Brother.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.630
I don't hate humans.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.760
The only one I hate...

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.640
is you, Luke!

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.270
Wake up, Vlad.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.520
Don't tell me you're gone, too.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:11:59.490
That hurts.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.970
It's an emergency, Vlad. Luke-san's missing.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:07.530
I baked some cookies for him, 
so I was looking for him.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.110
Why didn't you come to me first?

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:11.750
What?

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:15.330
I think you should consider yourself lucky.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:18.460
Hey!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.840
What does that mean?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.910
Luke's probably out hitting 
on some woman at a pub.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.890
He has the day off today.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.310
But he was acting strange earlier.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:31.480
He promised he'd rescue Shinyao himself.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.990
He seemed so serious.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.310
He's so easy to read.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:40.250
Does he know where the enemy is?

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.770
How did he find them?

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:45.110
Why didn't he tell us?

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.690
I have to look for him.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.540
Wait.

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:50.490
You may be right.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:55.120
Luke may have gone to settle 
things alone without telling us.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.590
Why?

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:57.330
Who knows?

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:00.220
Maybe he didn't want you to worry.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:01.920
I didn't ask him to do this!

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.630
It doesn't make sense for one person 
to sacrifice themselves to save another.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.850
You're one to talk.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:12.320
It's way less dangerous 
than going by yourself.

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:14.980
And besides, we're not people.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.440
Aw, jeez!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.980
How are you all so calm?

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.450
You really do act with your 
heart instead of your head, too.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:26.410
Toryu.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.180
Take all the bullets you can.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.750
You've gotten weak, brother.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.710
My eyes have been opened to peace.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:46.070
You still believe in a world where 
humans and Umbra can live together?

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.970
What are you, a priest?

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.090
No.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:53.810
It starts with respecting 
each other's territory.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.770
Why don't you come to the café
 and hear all about it?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.980
We've got warm food.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:03.370
Unfortunately, I don't believe in any god.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:07.070
What do you follow now, then?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.490
I don't need to tell you.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.670
This is goodbye, Broth—

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:21.270
Are you getting back at me 
for destroying your village?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.500
How tasteful of you.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.550
No! This is...

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:27.580
This was you, wasn't it?

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:29.680
Don't mess with me! Stay out of my way!

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:35.640
Since the person I want isn't there,
it's pointless to continue fighting.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:41.230
Take care of that pest so 
we can get out of here.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:44.610
Wait! Don't!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.260
What?

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.710
Thank you, Toryu-san.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:00.670
Miss!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.410
I see.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.550
You... You...

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:07.670
You're Baileu Ton!

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.810
If you really want to save your friend,

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:22.700
focus your thoughts on that 
ring and touch your own shadow.

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.190
My shadow?

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:27.800
Then Rijan will protect you.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.740
It really worked.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.850
I was expecting it to fail.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.710
I owe Wayne a pound.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:43.050
I'm doing my best over here!

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.070
Don't wager on it!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:46.000
Vlad.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.210
Sorry. We followed you.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:52.150
I thought I lost you.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:56.060
You can understand our signals?

00:15:56.230 --> 00:16:00.770
I don't understand the vulgar 
language of the wolves.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.730
But for a bat like myself,

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:08.850
determining your location based on 
your sound waves is a piece of cake.

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:10.530
You cheater.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:14.370
Really? You came to save him?

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.510
I didn't want to,

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:20.840
but there was a fool who 
refused to abandon a friend.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:24.040
A friend, huh? That's a laugh.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:28.000
He's a traitor. Can you really trust him?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.870
Of course I can.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:30.800
Why?

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:37.030
Because he values his friends 
enough to reminisce about the past

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:39.060
with a weakling like you.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.080
What was that?

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:47.110
Let me and Toryu handle the grunts.

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:51.740
Find your friend. She should be nearby.

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:53.180
Got it.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:54.550
And Luke...

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.910
Yeah. Thanks, guys.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:00.620
Now I don't have to worry about holding back!

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:01.440
What?

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:15.820
Shinyao! Shinyao!

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:17.890
Shinyao!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:23.070
Ton! I'm here, Ton!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.200
Shinyao!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.300
You finally found her, Ton.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:29.110
Yeah.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.070
Why won't you kill me?

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.910
I told you, I love peace now.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.080
Then we really should die.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.220
To humans, Umbra are trouble.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:46.480
We create fear.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:48.930
There's no reason to let us live.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.040
Chris.

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:55.470
Wait there, Shinyao! I'm coming!

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.930
Don't do anything crazy, Ton!

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:02.680
Come, Chris.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:04.480
Come with me.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:07.590
Never.

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:08.400
What?

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:11.190
You and the Twilights...

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.630
I'll never accept you!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.330
Chris!

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:16.570
Not good.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.370
Ton, have her jump!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.530
I'll catch her!

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:26.620
Jump, Shinyao! Trust me!

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.940
Toryu, shoot the wolf once she jumps.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.380
Don't let him get close.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:34.380
Got it.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.590
Wait!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.040
Hold on!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:37.970
Chris is...

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.340
Chris is...

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:10.290
Shinyao!

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:12.130
Shinyao!

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:15.200
Shinyao!

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:21.200
Well, I suppose disappointments 
are part of life.

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:26.060
Besides, I have my next method.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:31.850
And that toy still seems to be functional.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:40.900
Sorry.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.110
For what?

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:47.420
That was our chance to rescue 
your friend, and I ruined it.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:50.850
Well... I can't blame you.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:51.500
Why not?

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:56.240
You were trying to save Chris, right?

00:19:56.750 --> 00:20:00.640
It's the same as my desire to save Shinyao.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:03.750
We grew up together in the village.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:08.100
I don't remember how we were born.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:13.520
But as long as I can remember, 
we've been together.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.130
But since the incident—

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.150
No. Because of me...

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:25.840
In a language only I'd understand, 
Chris left me a message.

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:29.640
"I'll protect her no matter what happens."

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:31.040
That's great.

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:35.000
Then Shinyao will be fine 
as long as she's with him.

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.590
You trust him?

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.090
Maybe it's because he's your friend.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.070
We'll get her back together.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.080
Yeah, miss.

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.640
Actually, can I call you Ton?

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:48.310
That means you see me as a friend, right?

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:49.970
You're not hitting on me?

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.290
I'm not so sure.

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:55.150
Happily-smiling girls are my favorite prey.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.690
No!

00:22:35.120 --> 00:23:32.140
<b>Phantom Twilight 
Plus</b>

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.220
Phantom in the Twilight Plus!

00:22:38.110 --> 00:22:42.340
In this episode we'll be introducing 
the runaway train of the Twilights.

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:44.220
Luke Bowen here.

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:46.340
What's with the catchphrase?

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:50.890
Looking back on your actions in this 
episode, can you really object?

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:53.770
Normally I assume a human form,

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:57.630
but I'm a super powerful Umbra who can 
turn into a wolf when he needs to.

00:22:57.630 --> 00:22:58.690
You glossed over it.

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:00.520
You just casually glossed over what I said.

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:03.410
I'm amazing when I transform.

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:09.660
I'm a super fast and super powerful wolf
 with the power of regeneration.

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:12.930
As in the legend of the wolfman, 
you're weak to silver weapons.

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:15.860
Yeah. It costs a lot of money to defeat me.

00:23:15.860 --> 00:23:17.120
Prepare yourself.

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.180
Currently the wolfmen live in hidden 
villages in the countryside.

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:23.710
As a city-dweller, Luke is unorthodox.

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:28.340
Chris and I used to live in a village, 
but it was destroyed in a certain incident.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:29.350
What incident?

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:31.370
Who cares? Don't sweat the details.

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:34.410
Your brother seemed rather interested in them.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:50.070
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:38.810
Shinyao disappeared with Chris 
and we lost their trail,

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:42.650
but we're given no reprieve as we're 
attacked by a new and true enemy.

00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:44.360
His goal is determined by—

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.750
Toryu! Should you be calling 
anyone a runaway train?

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:50.070
<b>
Episode 4 Important Friends</b>

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:49.700
Next time: Important Friends.
